No, that's a good excuse you make for them, but the
confusion in Google Groups software between email
and Usenet news articles is profound and runs right
to the core.

That line isn't just a matter of "badly worded";
they really _meant_ "email" rather than "email
address".

The confusion comes in part because of gmail, they
now have a moderately good (but broken and unusable,
last time I tried it) email interface that will let
you send your response to the OP instead of the
newsgroup, and CC/BCC it to yourself if you want
[but still won't let you both mail and post the same
body text, sadly; a few posters _request_ that
responses to their articles also be emailed to them,
though most who mention the issue request the exact
opposite].

The same tool is thus doing email and news, they've
just never realized that all the email-ish stuff
needs to happen downstream of where the decision to
post or email a response takes effect, and so they
do ridiculous stuff like extra-quoting "From " or
"from " at the head of a line in posted news, a
quoting only needed for email, where that's a magic
token separating multiple emails sent in a stream,
not for news, where the similar magic token is
spelled "path ".

They've actually _fixed_ some of the bugs I reported
in this area of confusion between postings and
emails, the interface now says "Your posting was
successful" where it once said something to which I
obected to them that indicated that your email had
been sent.

However, they've replaced "post" with "send" (where
a more neutral word like "commit" would serve either
purpose), and left intact / added more email versus
posting confusions in the newly (inappropriately)
promoted beta release software.

